 # T-202 Customers connect their own Gmail
@@ -12,3 +12,60 @@ Pilot customers should be able to connect their own Gmail account so the
 support agent can read their order-confirmation emails when they ask about an
 order. Each customer connects only their own mailbox and can disconnect it.
 The pilot starts with 30 customers in three weeks.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Run on 2026-10-09 by a coding agent (adk-engineer → adk-tool-auth-and-secrets).
+Profile assumed: pilot/MVP (30 external customers, 3 weeks).
+
+**Estimate check.** The acceptance needs much more than 1-2 h: there is no
+customer sign-in or gateway in this repo; the connect/callback/disconnect
+routes, durable token and connection stores, and a real ADK Runner test are
+missing; and `gmail.readonly` is a Google *restricted* scope, so a public app
+needs OAuth verification plus a third-party security assessment (a calendar
+wait of weeks). This change is the largest useful local slice; the rest is
+proposed as tickets/T-203.md.
+
+**Built (local, offline-tested):**
+- `support_agent/gmail_connect.py`: per-customer consent (single-use state,
+  PKCE S256, browser binding, principal/client/redirect checks, granted-scope
+  check, `access_type=offline`), connection index with revision compare-and-set,
+  refresh coordination (transient failure keeps consent; `invalid_grant` marks
+  only the failing revision `reauth_required`; stale refresh cannot reactivate),
+  local-first disconnect then Google revoke with recorded failures, and an
+  httpx Google provider (not exercised live).
+- `support_agent/gmail_tools.py`: `find_order_confirmations(order_id)`. The
+  mailbox owner comes from the ADK session `user_id`, never from the model.
+  It returns sender, date, subject (capped) and order IDs extracted in code,
+  never the email body. Order-ID argument validated before any provider call;
+  resource 401 → one refresh and retry; 429/403/5xx → `unavailable` with
+  consent kept; not connected → `authorization_required`.
+- `support_agent/agent.py`: tool added to `root_agent` plus one instruction sentence.
+- `support_agent/__init__.py`: `root_agent` now loaded lazily so tests run without google-adk.
+
+**Checks:**
+- `python3.11 -m unittest tests.test_gmail_connect tests.test_gmail_tools -v`:
+  26 passed, 1 skipped (ADK declaration test: google-adk not installed). Offline,
+  with a fake Google provider/HTTP transport.
+- `python3 (3.9) -m pytest -q tests/test_tools.py`: 1 passed (it failed to
+  collect before the `__init__` change because google-adk is absent).
+- Static inspector (`--expect-adk 2.8.0`): complete, `static_pins_match`, no observations.
+- **Not run:** ADK declaration test; real Runner orchestration with a model
+  double; live Google consent/refresh/revoke; Gmail API; `adk web`/Cloud Run
+  loading of `root_agent` through the lazy `__init__`; restart or multiple replicas.
+
+**Controls deliberately left out at this profile (added in T-203 or before external launch):**
+in-memory stores only (not safe on Cloud Run with more than one instance or a restart);
+no gateway routes/cookies; no Secret Manager wiring for the client secret; no
+encrypted token store; no revocation reconciliation worker; no OAuth callback
+access-log scrubbing; no per-customer Gmail call budget. Security: `root_agent`
+now holds customer mailbox data *and* `send_email`/refund hand-off. Returning
+no bodies narrows but does not remove the injection path (subjects are
+attacker-controlled). This is a T-104 (security review) blocker before external customers.
+
+**Human effort still owed for this change:** about 1-1.5 h to review and verify.
+Check the consent/refresh/disconnect state machine in `gmail_connect.py`, check that the returned
+fields are acceptable to show the model, and run the full test suite with google-adk 2.8.0 on Python 3.11.
+Confirm that the deployed entrypoint still finds `root_agent`.
+Person-only steps: create the OAuth client and consent screen in Google Cloud Console, decide
+between Testing mode and verification, and add the pilot customers as test users.
